    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 45 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `checkDigit` field to the owner response that returns a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` default method that runs the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits of `customerCode` (returning `null` when the code is absent, e.g. seed data, consistent with how `membershipNumber` is handled).\n\nThe Luhn computation mirrors the reference `luhn(...)` helper in the test's `AcceptanceBase`, so the test's recomputation from the returned `customerCode` matches the asserted digit exactly.",
